# Copy to `.env.test`. Loaded on top of `.env` when APP_ENV=test
# (`npm test`, `npm run dev:test`, `npm run start:test`). Override only what
# differs for the test environment — most importantly the database.
#
# HOW THE TEST SUITE USES THE DB ---------------------------------------------
# The harness (supabase/api/tests/setup/global.ts) creates an isolated `test`
# SCHEMA, applies db/schema.sql into it, seeds users, runs the suite, then
# DROPs the schema on teardown. So it is safe to point DATABASE_URL at ANY
# database (even dev) — only the `test` schema is touched; `public` is never
# modified.
#
# TWO HARD REQUIREMENTS for DATABASE_URL below:
#   1. Use the Neon UNPOOLED (direct) host — i.e. WITHOUT `-pooler` in the
#      hostname. The pooled endpoint REJECTS the search_path startup option
#      with: "unsupported startup parameter in options: search_path".
#   2. Append the search_path option so BOTH the harness and the app's pg pool
#      resolve to the `test` schema:
#          ?options=-c%20search_path%3Dtest
#      (use `&options=...` if the connection string already has a `?query`).
#
# Example — note: no `-pooler`, and the trailing options param:
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@ep-xxxx.eu-central-1.aws.neon.tech/dbname?sslmode=require&options=-c%20search_path%3Dtest

# JWT_SECRET is inherited from `.env`; set here only to sign test sessions with
# a different key.
# JWT_SECRET=

# Run the test API on its own port so it can run beside prod (:4000).
PORT=4001

# Irrelevant to `npm test` (supertest calls the app in-process), but handy for a
# standalone test API. `*` is fine for local test; never in prod.
CORS_ORIGINS=*

# Payment tests use the MoMo mock; demo mode makes disbursement deterministic
# (no real MTN calls).
MOMO_MODE=demo

# Same for BK (UrubutoPay): force deterministic mock mode in tests even if a
# real URUBUTOPAY_API_KEY is set in the base `.env` (no real sandbox calls).
URUBUTOPAY_MODE=demo
